{
  "_doc": "ci-oops class a (infra): a red that is the machine's, not the code's. act_retry.py re-runs it on a fresh runner; it wakes no one. Owner: helper 1a (lane ci-self-heal). Each rule's `fixture` names its real log excerpt under tools/ci-oops/fixtures/infra/. Regexes are re.search, case-insensitive, per log line (oops_core.py). Rules that read a line a test could also print (OOM, disk, network, 5xx, cache, download, timeout, artifacts) carry `none`: the code-failure markers of cmux classify_failures (a failed test, a compile error), which outweigh them, so a test's expected ENOSPC in a red test job stays the code's.",
  "rules": [
    {
      "id": "infra.runner_shutdown",
      "class": "infra",
      "any": [
        "The runner has received a shutdown signal",
        "Runner .* (?:was|has been) (?:stopped|terminated|deprovisioned)"
      ],
      "why": "the runner was stopped mid-job (preemption, host restart, Blacksmith reclaim)"
    },
    {
      "id": "infra.runner_lost",
      "class": "infra",
      "any": [
        "The hosted runner encountered an error",
        "The hosted runner: .* lost communication",
        "The self-hosted runner: .* lost communication with the server",
        "lost communication with the server"
      ],
      "why": "the runner went away: GitHub fails the job after 10 minutes without it"
    },
    {
      "id": "infra.not_acquired",
      "class": "infra",
      "any": [
        "The job was not acquired by Runner of type",
        "was not acquired by Runner"
      ],
      "why": "GitHub handed the job to a runner that never took it"
    },
    {
      "id": "infra.runner_refused",
      "class": "infra",
      "any": [
        "recent account payments have failed",
        "spending limit needs to be increased",
        "The job was not started because",
        "refused at setup by its runner",
        "No runner matching the specified labels was found"
      ],
      "why": "the job was refused before it started (billing-refused hosted runner, no runner for its label, or the runner's own setup refusal): never the PR's red. act_retry waits while RUNNER_POOLS still names the dead label (hq#14387 run 44517256143, hq#14433 run 44520476170, 2026-11-19)",
      "fixture": "runner_refused_billing.log"
    },
    {
      "id": "infra.stale_checkout",
      "class": "infra",
      "when": [
        "checkout_failed"
      ],
      "any": [
        "not uptodate; will not remove from working tree",
        "Checking out the ref .* failed because the working tree is not clean"
      ],
      "why": "the checkout step failed on a reused runner's dirty workspace (cmux#47889 job 136241035294, 2026-11-20): runner state, not the PR. The same lines under a checkout that went on are git's warnings and blame nothing",
      "fixture": "stale_checkout.log"
    },
    {
      "id": "infra.no_step_ran",
      "class": "infra",
      "when": [
        "no_step_ran"
      ],
      "why": "the job failed before any workflow step ran: its runner died or was never set up"
    },
    {
      "id": "infra.setup_refused",
      "class": "infra",
      "when": [
        "setup_failed"
      ],
      "why": "the runner's own setup step failed (glaeda's job-started hook refusing a busy host, an image pull)"
    },
    {
      "id": "infra.oom",
      "class": "infra",
      "any": [
        "Out of memory: Killed process",
        "oom-kill",
        "OOMKilled",
        "\\bKilled\\b.*signal 9|signal: killed|SIGKILL",
        "Process completed with exit code 137",
        "LLVM ERROR: out of memory",
        "fatal error: runtime: out of memory",
        "JavaScript heap out of memory",
        "error: could not compile .* \\(signal: 9, SIGKILL",
        "c\\+\\+: fatal error: Killed signal terminated program",
        "ld(?:\\.lld)?: error: .*(?:Cannot allocate memory|out of memory)"
      ],
      "retries": 1,
      "why": "the kernel killed the job's process for memory: one re-run, then it stays red (a bigger rung, not a third try)",
      "none": [
        "error\\[E\\d{4}\\]",
        "^error: could not compile .*due to",
        "test result: FAILED",
        "^\\s*FAIL(?:ED)?[: ]",
        "^FAILED \\((?:failures|errors)=",
        "^(?:FAIL|ERROR): test\\w* \\(",
        "^\\(fail\\) ",
        "AssertionError",
        "assertion .*failed",
        "panicked at",
        "error TS\\d+:",
        "\\S+\\.(?:swift|m|mm|c|h|ts|tsx|js|py|rs|zig):\\d+:\\d+: error: ",
        "\\.swift:\\d+: error: -\\[",
        "^✘ (?:Test|Suite) .+ (?:recorded an issue|failed after)",
        "^RATCHET_NEW_FAILURE ",
        "^--- FAIL: ",
        "^FAIL\\t",
        "^FAIL$",
        "^panic: "
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "infra.disk_full",
      "class": "infra",
      "any": [
        "No space left on device",
        "ENOSPC",
        "You are running out of disk space",
        "System.IO.IOException: There is not enough space on the disk"
      ],
      "why": "the runner's disk filled. Three or more ENOSPC lines outweigh the test failures the full disk caused (hq run 44508779820, 2026-11-19: two test jobs, 41 and 17 failures, all ENOSPC); one line is a test's own, and the code markers keep it the code's",
      "none": [
        "error\\[E\\d{4}\\]",
        "^error: could not compile .*due to",
        "test result: FAILED",
        "^\\s*FAIL(?:ED)?[: ]",
        "^FAILED \\((?:failures|errors)=",
        "^(?:FAIL|ERROR): test\\w* \\(",
        "^\\(fail\\) ",
        "AssertionError",
        "assertion .*failed",
        "panicked at",
        "error TS\\d+:",
        "\\S+\\.(?:swift|m|mm|c|h|ts|tsx|js|py|rs|zig):\\d+:\\d+: error: ",
        "\\.swift:\\d+: error: -\\[",
        "^✘ (?:Test|Suite) .+ (?:recorded an issue|failed after)",
        "^RATCHET_NEW_FAILURE ",
        "^--- FAIL: ",
        "^FAIL\\t",
        "^FAIL$",
        "^panic: "
      ],
      "min": 3,
      "fixture": "disk_full.log"
    },
    {
      "id": "infra.network",
      "class": "infra",
      "any": [
        "Could not resolve host",
        "Temporary failure in name resolution",
        "getaddrinfo (?:EAI_AGAIN|ENOTFOUND)",
        "\\bECONNRESET\\b",
        "\\bETIMEDOUT\\b",
        "\\bECONNREFUSED\\b.*(?:registry|github|npmjs|crates\\.io|ghcr|docker)",
        "Connection reset by peer",
        "TLS handshake timeout",
        "net/http: request canceled while waiting for connection",
        "SSL_ERROR_SYSCALL",
        "OpenSSL SSL_(?:read|connect): .*(?:Connection reset|SSL_ERROR)",
        "RPC failed; curl \\d+",
        "fatal: unable to access 'https://.*': (?:Failed to connect|Could not resolve|Recv failure|The requested URL returned error: 5\\d\\d)",
        "error: RPC failed",
        "early EOF",
        "Failed to connect to .* port \\d+",
        "spurious network error",
        "failed to download from `https://"
      ],
      "why": "a network fault between the runner and a registry, GitHub or a mirror",
      "none": [
        "error\\[E\\d{4}\\]",
        "^error: could not compile .*due to",
        "test result: FAILED",
        "^\\s*FAIL(?:ED)?[: ]",
        "^FAILED \\((?:failures|errors)=",
        "^(?:FAIL|ERROR): test\\w* \\(",
        "^\\(fail\\) ",
        "AssertionError",
        "assertion .*failed",
        "panicked at",
        "error TS\\d+:",
        "\\S+\\.(?:swift|m|mm|c|h|ts|tsx|js|py|rs|zig):\\d+:\\d+: error: ",
        "\\.swift:\\d+: error: -\\[",
        "^✘ (?:Test|Suite) .+ (?:recorded an issue|failed after)",
        "^RATCHET_NEW_FAILURE ",
        "^--- FAIL: ",
        "^FAIL\\t",
        "^FAIL$",
        "^panic: "
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "infra.upstream_5xx",
      "class": "infra",
      "any": [
        "(?:HTTP|status|status code|returned error:?) ?(?:502|503|504)\\b",
        "\\b(?:502 Bad Gateway|503 Service (?:Temporarily )?Unavailable|504 Gateway Time-?out)\\b",
        "Internal Server Error.*(?:api\\.github\\.com|codeload|objects\\.githubusercontent|pipelines\\.actions)",
        "Response status code does not indicate success: 5\\d\\d",
        "toomanyrequests: You have reached your pull rate limit",
        "Failed to (?:download|fetch) action",
        "Unable to (?:download|resolve) action",
        "An error occurred while (?:downloading|provisioning)"
      ],
      "why": "GitHub, a registry or an action download answered 5xx or rate-limited the runner",
      "none": [
        "error\\[E\\d{4}\\]",
        "^error: could not compile .*due to",
        "test result: FAILED",
        "^\\s*FAIL(?:ED)?[: ]",
        "^FAILED \\((?:failures|errors)=",
        "^(?:FAIL|ERROR): test\\w* \\(",
        "^\\(fail\\) ",
        "AssertionError",
        "assertion .*failed",
        "panicked at",
        "error TS\\d+:",
        "\\S+\\.(?:swift|m|mm|c|h|ts|tsx|js|py|rs|zig):\\d+:\\d+: error: ",
        "\\.swift:\\d+: error: -\\[",
        "^✘ (?:Test|Suite) .+ (?:recorded an issue|failed after)",
        "^RATCHET_NEW_FAILURE ",
        "^--- FAIL: ",
        "^FAIL\\t",
        "^FAIL$",
        "^panic: "
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "infra.cache_service",
      "class": "infra",
      "any": [
        "Failed to (?:restore|save) cache.*(?:5\\d\\d|timeout|ECONNRESET|socket hang up)",
        "Cache service responded with 5\\d\\d",
        "Our services aren't available right now",
        "reserveCache failed",
        "getCacheEntry failed",
        "sccache: error: (?:Server startup failed|Timed out waiting for server)",
        "sccache: Compile terminated by signal",
        "stickydisk.*(?:failed|timeout|error)",
        "blacksmith.*(?:cache|sticky).*(?:failed|unavailable|timed out)"
      ],
      "none": [
        "error\\[E\\d{4}\\]",
        "^error: could not compile .*due to",
        "test result: FAILED",
        "^\\s*FAIL(?:ED)?[: ]",
        "^FAILED \\((?:failures|errors)=",
        "^(?:FAIL|ERROR): test\\w* \\(",
        "^\\(fail\\) ",
        "AssertionError",
        "assertion .*failed",
        "panicked at",
        "error TS\\d+:",
        "\\S+\\.(?:swift|m|mm|c|h|ts|tsx|js|py|rs|zig):\\d+:\\d+: error: ",
        "\\.swift:\\d+: error: -\\[",
        "^✘ (?:Test|Suite) .+ (?:recorded an issue|failed after)",
        "^RATCHET_NEW_FAILURE ",
        "^--- FAIL: ",
        "^FAIL\\t",
        "^FAIL$",
        "^panic: "
      ],
      "why": "the cache service or sticky disk failed, not the code"
    },
    {
      "id": "infra.toolchain_download",
      "class": "infra",
      "any": [
        "error: failed to download",
        "rustup: .*(?:could not download|error downloading)",
        "error: component download failed",
        "Unable to (?:download|fetch|install) (?:Node|Bun|Go|Xcode|the toolchain)",
        "zig: .*(?:download|fetch) failed",
        "curl: \\((?:6|7|18|28|35|52|56)\\)",
        "wget: unable to resolve host"
      ],
      "why": "a toolchain or dependency download failed in setup",
      "none": [
        "error\\[E\\d{4}\\]",
        "^error: could not compile .*due to",
        "test result: FAILED",
        "^\\s*FAIL(?:ED)?[: ]",
        "^FAILED \\((?:failures|errors)=",
        "^(?:FAIL|ERROR): test\\w* \\(",
        "^\\(fail\\) ",
        "AssertionError",
        "assertion .*failed",
        "panicked at",
        "error TS\\d+:",
        "\\S+\\.(?:swift|m|mm|c|h|ts|tsx|js|py|rs|zig):\\d+:\\d+: error: ",
        "\\.swift:\\d+: error: -\\[",
        "^✘ (?:Test|Suite) .+ (?:recorded an issue|failed after)",
        "^RATCHET_NEW_FAILURE ",
        "^--- FAIL: ",
        "^FAIL\\t",
        "^FAIL$",
        "^panic: "
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "infra.timeout",
      "class": "infra",
      "any": [
        "The job running on runner .* has exceeded the maximum execution time",
        "has exceeded the maximum execution time of \\d+ minutes"
      ],
      "when": [
        "cancelled_mid_step"
      ],
      "why": "the job ran out of time with a step cancelled under it: a stalled runner or pool more often than a hang; one re-run, then it stays red",
      "retries": 1,
      "none": [
        "error\\[E\\d{4}\\]",
        "^error: could not compile .*due to",
        "test result: FAILED",
        "^\\s*FAIL(?:ED)?[: ]",
        "^FAILED \\((?:failures|errors)=",
        "^(?:FAIL|ERROR): test\\w* \\(",
        "^\\(fail\\) ",
        "AssertionError",
        "assertion .*failed",
        "panicked at",
        "error TS\\d+:",
        "\\S+\\.(?:swift|m|mm|c|h|ts|tsx|js|py|rs|zig):\\d+:\\d+: error: ",
        "\\.swift:\\d+: error: -\\[",
        "^✘ (?:Test|Suite) .+ (?:recorded an issue|failed after)",
        "^RATCHET_NEW_FAILURE ",
        "^--- FAIL: ",
        "^FAIL\\t",
        "^FAIL$",
        "^panic: "
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "infra.runner_hook_refused",
      "class": "infra",
      "any": [
        "glaeda-cmux-runner-hook: refused: "
      ],
      "why": "an owned runner's job-started hook refused the job (host busy or out of capacity); from cmux classify_failures runner-hook-refused"
    },
    {
      "id": "infra.product_restore_failed",
      "class": "infra",
      "any": [
        "^CMUX_TEST_PRODUCT_RESTORE \\{.*\"outcome\": \"failure\"",
        "Unexpected app-host preparation outcome",
        "^Could not take this Mac's gui token for the app-host tests \\(take-gui exited "
      ],
      "why": "the runner did not restore the compiled products or prepare the app-host home; from cmux classify_failures"
    },
    {
      "id": "infra.mixed_products",
      "class": "infra",
      "any": [
        "dyld\\[\\d+\\]: Symbol not found: "
      ],
      "why": "a binary loaded a framework from another build (stale products on the runner); from cmux classify_failures",
      "none": [
        "error\\[E\\d{4}\\]",
        "^error: could not compile .*due to",
        "test result: FAILED",
        "^\\s*FAIL(?:ED)?[: ]",
        "^FAILED \\((?:failures|errors)=",
        "^(?:FAIL|ERROR): test\\w* \\(",
        "^\\(fail\\) ",
        "AssertionError",
        "assertion .*failed",
        "panicked at",
        "error TS\\d+:",
        "\\S+\\.(?:swift|m|mm|c|h|ts|tsx|js|py|rs|zig):\\d+:\\d+: error: ",
        "\\.swift:\\d+: error: -\\[",
        "^✘ (?:Test|Suite) .+ (?:recorded an issue|failed after)",
        "^RATCHET_NEW_FAILURE ",
        "^--- FAIL: ",
        "^FAIL\\t",
        "^FAIL$",
        "^panic: "
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "infra.xcode_pin_missing",
      "class": "infra",
      "any": [
        "\\[cmux-ci machine: xcode-pin-missing\\]",
        "^Pinned Xcode developer dir (?:does not exist|has no usable macOS SDK): ",
        "^This macOS \\d+ runner has no Xcode \\S+, the version scripts/ci/xcode-pins\\.txt pins"
      ],
      "retries": 1,
      "why": "the runner lacks the Xcode the job pins: a re-run lands on another runner; from cmux classify_failures"
    },
    {
      "id": "infra.artifact_download",
      "class": "infra",
      "any": [
        "^Unable to download artifact\\(s\\): .*Artifact download failed after \\d+ retries",
        "Failed to (?:download|upload) artifact.*(?:5\\d\\d|ECONNRESET|timeout|socket hang up)",
        "Unable to (?:upload|finalize) artifact.*(?:5\\d\\d|timeout)"
      ],
      "none": [
        "error\\[E\\d{4}\\]",
        "^error: could not compile .*due to",
        "test result: FAILED",
        "^\\s*FAIL(?:ED)?[: ]",
        "^FAILED \\((?:failures|errors)=",
        "^(?:FAIL|ERROR): test\\w* \\(",
        "^\\(fail\\) ",
        "AssertionError",
        "assertion .*failed",
        "panicked at",
        "error TS\\d+:",
        "\\S+\\.(?:swift|m|mm|c|h|ts|tsx|js|py|rs|zig):\\d+:\\d+: error: ",
